  "description": "Answer questions from what the wiki already knows, citing the wiki pages behind every claim so the user can open and verify them. Reads only — never changes the wiki unless the user explicitly asks to save the answer as a page. Use this whenever the user asks a question whose answer should come from the wiki — even if they don't say \"ask\". Also fires for: \"what does the wiki say about X\", \"compare X and Y from what we've ingested\", \"summarize the wiki's coverage of X\", \"what concepts relate to Y\", \"find all sources that mention Z\", \"what have we learned about X\", or any synthesis or retrieval request over accumulated wiki content. If a question could be answered from raw/ but isn't in the wiki yet, surface the gap, list the matching raw/ files so the user can open them directly, and suggest /lumi-ingest instead of reading raw/.",
